course: dictionary
lesson: 12388
title: Cultivate: to grow and to build with care
level: primary-5
stars: 1
explain: «Cultivate» is a word with more than one meaning. Its main idea is to prepare land and grow things, or to build something slowly and with care. The clues in the sentence tell you which meaning is right. «The farmers cultivated the land before they planted the wheat.» Digging and planting come before growing, so cultivate means to prepare the ground for crops.
explain: The same word can work in other places. «Maya cultivated a friendship with the new girl by sharing her lunch every day.» No one is digging here. Sharing lunch every day shows slow, careful effort, so cultivate means to build something up over time.
explain: In science, the word means something different again. «Scientists cultivated bacteria in a dish to see how they grew.» The scientists grew the bacteria on purpose, in a lab. Always ask: what is being grown or built, and how? The clues will show you which meaning fits.
fact: Cultivate is a verb. Its other forms are cultivates, cultivated and cultivating.
fact: «Cultivate» means to prepare land and use it for growing crops, such as digging, planting and looking after it.
fact: «Cultivate» also means to build something up slowly with care, such as a skill, a habit or a friendship.
fact: «Cultivated» fields are fields that have been prepared and planted by people.
fact: In science, to cultivate means to grow bacteria or cells in a lab.
exercise: «The farmers cultivated the land before they planted the wheat.» What does cultivated mean here? | Covered the land with snow | Sold the land to a shop | Walked across the land quickly | *Prepared the land and used it for growing crops
exercise: «Maya cultivated a friendship with the new girl.» Which word shows that Maya built something up slowly? | girl | Maya | *cultivated | new
exercise: «Scientists cultivated bacteria in a dish.» What did the scientists grow? | Wheat in a field | Rice in a bowl | Stones in a box | *Bacteria in a lab
test: «Early people began to cultivate rice, so they could settle in villages.» Why did cultivating rice help them? | They could travel faster | They could find gold | *They could stay in one place and grow their own food | They could fly
test: Lily wants to cultivate good habits, like reading every night. What does cultivate mean here? | To hide quickly | To cut down or remove | To sell in a shop | *To build up slowly with care
exam: A gardener says «I will cultivate these beds this spring», meaning she will dig the soil and plant seeds. Which meaning fits best? | Break the beds into pieces | Sleep in the garden | Forget about the beds | *Prepare the soil and plant seeds
